    "the_symmetric_half_is_a_trapezoid_remainder": {
      "identity": "eps_k + eps_(N-1-k) = (1/2)[f(th) + f(th+h)] - (1/h) int_th^{th+h} f,  f = log(2 sin), h = pi/N",
      "derivation": "substitute s_k = (N/pi)Lambda(th) - (1/2)log(2N sin th) + eps_k into the reflection and use Lambda(pi-x) = -Lambda(x); everything else cancels",
      "consequence": "the symmetric half of (A)'s error is O(h^2 csc^2 th), already sharper than the O(1/N) claimed. All of (A)'s difficulty is in the ANTISYMMETRIC half",
